.TL
Harbor Lights Survey Report
.AU
Field Team North
.NH 1
Overview
.PP
The harbor survey counted seventeen working lights along the north breakwater.
Every light was checked at dusk and again before dawn, and the keepers logged
fuel, lens condition and visibility in nautical miles.
.PP
Weather stayed calm for most of the week, although fog rolled in on Thursday
morning and delayed the second inspection of the outer markers.
.NH 2
Equipment
.IP \(bu 3
Portable photometer with a calibrated filter set.
.IP \(bu 3
Two handheld radios tuned to the harbor channel.
.IP \(bu 3
A tide table printed for the current month.
.NH 1
Measurements
.TS
center box;
l l n.
