.TE
.PP
Range figures follow the international convention for nominal range at a
meteorological visibility of ten nautical miles.
.bp
.2C
.NH 1
Recommendations
.PP
Replace the cracked prism on the North Pier light before the winter season.
The keepers agreed that the replacement should be scheduled for a calm day,
because the gallery rail is exposed to spray when the wind comes from the east.
Spare parts are stored in the shed beside the fuel tanks.
.PP
Repaint the daymark on the Outer Mole tower. The current paint has faded to a
pale orange that blends with the rocks in late afternoon light, which makes
the tower hard to pick out from the approach channel.
.PP
Install a backup battery bank at the Fish Dock station so that the light keeps
running during the short outages that follow summer storms.
.PP
Keep the fog signal log in the same binder as the light log, so that every
watch can see both records at once and compare the timing of each event.
.PP
Train two more volunteers to read the photometer, because the current team
of three cannot cover every station during the busiest weeks of the year.
.PP
Order new gaskets for the lantern room doors before the end of the month.
